<back><div type="verses">
<lg label="2."><l>I’m mercy’s vessel, this I know,</l><l>For God has chosen me;</l><l>The riches of His glory shall</l><l>Thus manifested be.</l><l>Not him who wills can follow now</l><l>This way as yet unknown;</l><l>Not him who runs can yet pursue,</l><l>But to whom mercy’s shown.</l></lg>
<lg label="3."><l>My Father’s lovingkindness, ’tis,</l><l>That I am not consumed—</l><l>For His compassions never fail;</l><l>Each morning they are new.</l><l>Through His compassions day by day</l><l>I give myself to be</l><l>Transformed and built with other saints,</l><l>Christ’s Body thus to see.</l></lg>
</div>
</back>
</music></mei>
